 "description": "Octal bus transceiver, 3-state outputs",
 "drawer": [
  "Logic"
 ],
 "note": "Standard '245 pinout (1 DIR, 2-9 A1-A8, 10 GND, 11-18 B8-B1, 19 OE, 20 VCC) in every PDF: sn74hc245 p.3 (DB/DGV/DW/N/J/W/PW and FK, same numbers), sn74ahc245 p.3 (RKS VQFN same numbers, thermal pad), sn74ahct245 p.3 (RGY/RKS), sn74abt245b p.1 (RGY, FK), sn74lvc245a p.3 (RGY), sn74auc245 p.1 (RGY), sn74ac245 p.3 (DGS, RKS), sn74hcs245 p.3, sn74lv245a p.3, cy74fct245t p.1, cd74fct245 p.1, sn74ls245 p.3, sn74als245a p.1 (ALS and AS), sn74f245 p.1, sn74bct245 p.1, sn64bct245 p.1, sn74alvc245 p.1, sn74lvt245b p.1. Name aliases (same positions): CY74FCT245T names DIR 'T/R' and numbers the bits A0-A7/B0-B7; CD54/74AC(T)245 (p.3) and CD54/74HC(T)245 (p.3, drawing only) number the bits A0-A7/B0-B7. Function table identical in all PDFs: OE low + DIR low = B to A, OE low + DIR high = A to B, OE high = isolation (sn74hc245 p.9, cd74ac245 p.11, cy74fct245t p.2, sn74lvc245a p.9 Table 1, ...). LS/ALS/AS/F/BCT parts have 3-state push-pull outputs like the rest.",
